{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Sated with favor.</b> That his land was sated with every desire of its inhabitants." "<b>The sea and the south he shall inherit.</b> The Sea of Kinneret fell in his portion, and he took the full extent of the territory of Herem to its south, to spread out vine-terraces and fish-ponds (Bava Kamma ch. 1)." "<b>He shall inherit.</b> A term of command, like ״עֲלֵה רֵשׁ״ (Deuteronomy 1). And the accent above on the רֵי״שׁ proves it — like סְלַח, יְדַע, לְקַח, שְׁמַע: when a ה׵א is added to them, the accent is above — סְלָחָה, יְדָעָה, לְקָחָה, שְׁמָעָה. So too here — יְרָשָׁה is a term of command. And in the Great Masorah we find, in the alphabetical list, that a term of command has its accent from above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:50.989398941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}